  "title": " ",
  "description": "The MNE-Sample-Data dataset is a simultaneous MEG and 60-channel EEG recording with an accompanying structural MRI, distributed with the MNE software. Checkerboard patterns were presented to the left and right visual fields, interleaved with tones to the left or right ear, and the subject responded to occasional smiley faces. It serves as a standard example dataset for demonstrating MEG/EEG analysis workflows, and FreeSurfer-derived anatomical surfaces are included.",
  "methods_description": "Data were acquired with a Neuromag Vectorview MEG system at the MGH/HMS/MIT Athinoula A. Martinos Center, with simultaneous 60-channel EEG. Structural MRI was acquired on a Siemens 1.5 T Sonata scanner using an MPRAGE sequence. Stimuli were checkerboards in the left or right visual field and tones to the left or right ear, with a 750 ms interstimulus interval. The subject pressed a key with the right index finger when a smiley face appeared at the center. FreeSurfer recon-all and MNE BEM and scalp surface tools were used to generate anatomical derivatives.",
